{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-14-Dec-2025-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 23, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The simplified value of 4 × ( 17 × ( 32 )) ÷ 12 + 26 − 41 is:", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "32", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": "36"}, {"n": 2, "text": "The marked price of a sofa is ₹331, which is 41% above the cost price. If the profit percent is 22%, find the discount percentage. (Rounded off to two decimal places)", "options": [{"text": "16.1%", "added": false}, {"text": "12.02%", "added": false}, {"text": "11.23%", "added": false}, {"text": "13.48%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "mp-sp-relation", "key_answer": "13.48%"}, {"n": 3, "text": "The diagonals of a rhombus are 24 cm and 7 cm. The perimeter of the rhombus is:", "options": [{"text": "48 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "46 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "50 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "52 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "polygons", "key_answer": "50 cm"}, {"n": 4, "text": "What is the third proportional to 16x2 and 20xy?", "options": [{"text": "27y2", "added": false}, {"text": "25y2", "added": false}, {"text": "22y2", "added": false}, {"text": "28y2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": "25y2"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The average of 12 numbers is 58. The average of the first 5 numbers is 55, and the average of the next 4 numbers is 62. If the 10th number is 10 less than the 11th number and is 5 more than the 12th number, then the average of the 11th and 10th numbers is:6560", "options": [{"text": "60", "added": false}, {"text": "61", "added": false}, {"text": "61.5", "added": false}, {"text": "60.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "61"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A, B and C can do a piece of work in 2, 20 and 20 days respectively. How long (in days) will they take to do thrice the same work, working together?", "options": [{"text": "5", "added": false}, {"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "10", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "5"}, {"n": 7, "text": "If the three digit number 7n4 is divisible by 6, then find the least possible value for n.", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "divisibility-rules", "key_answer": "1"}, {"n": 8, "text": "In △ ABC, BD ⟂ AC at D and ∠ DBC = 42°. E is a point on BC such that ∠ CAE = 24°. What is the measure of ∠ AEB?", "options": [{"text": "58°", "added": false}, {"text": "59°", "added": false}, {"text": "72°", "added": false}, {"text": "67°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "triangles", "key_answer": "72°"}, {"n": 9, "text": "Anmol and Ayushi together invested ₹41,400 in a business. At the end of the year, out of a total profit of ₹5,000, Anmol's share was ₹2,300. How much was Anmol's investment?", "options": [{"text": "₹20,105", "added": false}, {"text": "₹18,630", "added": false}, {"text": "₹17,095", "added": false}, {"text": "₹19,044", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹19,044"}, {"n": 10, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 2% of the voters did not cast their votes. Out of